## 2. Binomial Distribution

Let $X \sim \text{Binomial}(n = 20, p = 0.08)$, where $q = 1 - p = 0.92$.
$$P(X = k) = \binom{20}{k} (0.08)^k (0.92)^{20-k}$$

```{r}
n <- 20
p <- 0.08
```

### (a) Probability that exactly 2 requests are malicious: $P(X = 2)$

```{r}
p_eq_2 <- dbinom(2, size = n, prob = p)
```

$$P(X = 2) = \binom{20}{2} (0.08)^2 (0.92)^{18} = 190 \times 0.0064 \times 0.2229 \approx `r round(p_eq_2, 4)`$$

---

### (b) Probability that at least 3 requests are malicious: $P(X \ge 3)$

Using the complement:
$$P(X \ge 3) = 1 - [P(X = 0) + P(X = 1) + P(X = 2)]$$

```{r}
p0 <- dbinom(0, size = n, prob = p)
p1 <- dbinom(1, size = n, prob = p)
p2 <- dbinom(2, size = n, prob = p)
p_lt_3 <- pbinom(2, size = n, prob = p)
p_ge_3 <- pbinom(2, size = n, prob = p, lower.tail = FALSE)
```

Calculate individual terms:

* $P(X = 0) = \binom{20}{0} (0.08)^0 (0.92)^{20} \approx `r round(p0, 4)`$
* $P(X = 1) = \binom{20}{1} (0.08)^1 (0.92)^{19} = 20 \times 0.08 \times 0.2051 \approx `r round(p1, 4)`$
* $P(X = 2) \approx `r round(p2, 4)`$

Sum of $P(X < 3)$:
$$P(X < 3) = `r round(p0, 4)` + `r round(p1, 4)` + `r round(p2, 4)` = `r round(p_lt_3, 4)`$$

$$P(X \ge 3) = 1 - `r round(p_lt_3, 4)` = `r round(p_ge_3, 4)`$$

---

### (c) Mean and Standard Deviation

```{r}
mean_bin <- n * p
sd_bin <- sqrt(n * p * (1 - p))
```

* **Mean ($\mu$):**
  $$\mu = n \cdot p = 20 \times 0.08 = `r mean_bin`$$

* **Standard Deviation ($\sigma$):**
  $$\sigma = \sqrt{n \cdot p \cdot (1 - p)} = \sqrt{20 \times 0.08 \times 0.92} = \sqrt{1.472} \approx `r round(sd_bin, 4)`$$

