## 3. Poisson Distribution

### (a) Probability of receiving exactly 6 hits in 1 minute ($\lambda = 4.5$)

$$P(X = k) = \frac{e^{-\lambda} \lambda^k}{k!}$$

```{r}
lambda_1min <- 4.5
p_eq_6 <- dpois(6, lambda = lambda_1min)
```

$$P(X = 6) = \frac{e^{-4.5} (4.5)^6}{6!} = \frac{0.011109 \times 8303.7656}{720} \approx `r round(p_eq_6, 4)`$$

---

### (b) Probability of receiving at most 2 hits in 1 minute ($P(X \le 2)$)

$$P(X \le 2) = P(X = 0) + P(X = 1) + P(X = 2)$$

```{r}
poiss0 <- dpois(0, lambda = lambda_1min)
poiss1 <- dpois(1, lambda = lambda_1min)
poiss2 <- dpois(2, lambda = lambda_1min)
p_le_2 <- ppois(2, lambda = lambda_1min)
```

* $P(X = 0) = \frac{e^{-4.5} (4.5)^0}{0!} = e^{-4.5} \approx `r round(poiss0, 4)`$
* $P(X = 1) = \frac{e^{-4.5} (4.5)^1}{1!} = 4.5 \times 0.0111 \approx `r round(poiss1, 4)`$
* $P(X = 2) = \frac{e^{-4.5} (4.5)^2}{2!} = \frac{20.25}{2} \times 0.0111 \approx `r round(poiss2, 4)`$

$$P(X \le 2) = `r round(poiss0, 4)` + `r round(poiss1, 4)` + `r round(poiss2, 4)` = `r round(p_le_2, 4)`$$

---

### (c) Probability of receiving more than 10 hits in a 2-minute interval

Adjust rate for a $t = 2$ minute interval:
$$\lambda_{2\text{min}} = 4.5 \times 2 = 9.0$$

```{r}
lambda_2min <- 9.0
p_le_10 <- ppois(10, lambda = lambda_2min)
p_gt_10 <- ppois(10, lambda = lambda_2min, lower.tail = FALSE)
```

We seek $P(Y > 10) = 1 - P(Y \le 10)$, where $Y \sim \text{Poisson}(\lambda = 9)$:
$$P(Y \le 10) = \sum_{k=0}^{10} \frac{e^{-9} \cdot 9^k}{k!} \approx `r round(p_le_10, 4)`$$

$$P(Y > 10) = 1 - `r round(p_le_10, 4)` = `r round(p_gt_10, 4)`$$

