## 4. Continuous Probability & Normal Distribution

Let $X \sim \mathcal{N}(\mu = 120, \sigma = 15)$. Standardize to $Z = \frac{X - \mu}{\sigma}$.

```{r}
mu <- 120
sigma <- 15
```

### (a) Proportion of queries taking longer than 135 ms: $P(X > 135)$

```{r}
z135 <- (135 - mu) / sigma
p_gt_135 <- pnorm(135, mean = mu, sd = sigma, lower.tail = FALSE)
```

$$Z = \frac{135 - 120}{15} = `r z135`$$
$$P(X > 135) = P(Z > 1.0) = 1 - \Phi(1.0) = 1 - 0.8413 = `r round(p_gt_135, 4)`$$

---

### (b) Probability taking between 100 and 130 ms: $P(100 < X < 130)$

Standardize lower and upper bounds:

```{r}
z_low <- (100 - mu) / sigma
z_high <- (130 - mu) / sigma
phi_high <- pnorm(z_high)
phi_low <- pnorm(z_low)
p_between <- phi_high - phi_low
```

* $Z_1 = \frac{100 - 120}{15} = -\frac{20}{15} \approx `r round(z_low, 2)`$
* $Z_2 = \frac{130 - 120}{15} = \frac{10}{15} \approx `r round(z_high, 2)`$

Calculate probabilities from standard normal distribution tables:
$$\Phi(0.67) \approx `r round(phi_high, 4)`$$
$$\Phi(-1.33) \approx `r round(phi_low, 4)`$$

$$P(-1.33 < Z < 0.67) = \Phi(0.67) - \Phi(-1.33) = `r round(phi_high, 4)` - `r round(phi_low, 4)` = `r round(p_between, 4)`$$

---

### (c) 95th Percentile of query processing times

Find $x$ such that $P(X \le x) = 0.95$:

```{r}
z_95 <- qnorm(0.95)
p95 <- qnorm(0.95, mean = mu, sd = sigma)
```

From standard normal distribution tables, $P(Z \le z) = 0.95 \implies z \approx `r round(z_95, 3)`$.

Convert back to $X$:
$$x = \mu + z \cdot \sigma = 120 + (`r round(z_95, 3)` \times 15) = 120 + `r round(z_95 * 15, 3)` = `r round(p95, 3)`\text{ ms}$$
